            <div id="recipe-ingredients">
                <div id="recipe-ingredients" class="text-left mb-3 mb-lg-5">

    <h2 class="mb-3  text-capitalize">Ingredients</h2>

    <ul class="checklist-ul" id="recipe-ingredients-list">
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    1-2                    large                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>zucchini</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    1                    pound                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>spaghetti noodles</span>
            </li>
                                    <li class="lead mb-3 mt-4 font-weight-bold" style="list-style: none;margin-left:-1.5rem;">
                    SAUCE                </li>
                                        <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    1                    tablespoon                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>olive oil</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    2                    large                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>yellow onions, thinly sliced</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    2                    cloves                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>garlic, crushed</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    1                    can                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>crushed Roma tomatoes or whole plum tomatoes (28 oz)</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    1                    teaspoon                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>salt or to taste</span>
            </li>
                                    <li class="lead mb-3 mt-4 font-weight-bold" style="list-style: none;margin-left:-1.5rem;">
                    MEATBALLS                </li>
                                        <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    3                                    </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>slices of day old Italian bread</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    2                                    </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>eggs</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    1/4                    cup                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>Parmesan cheese, fat-free if desired, plus more for serving</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    2                    teaspoons                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>Italian seasoning</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    3                    cloves                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>garlic, crushed</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    2                    teaspoons                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>salt</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    3                    tablespoons                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>chopped fresh parsley</span>
            </li>
                                <li class="mb-3">
                <strong data-ingrient-quantity class="mr-1">
                    2                    pounds                </strong>
                <span data-ingredient-name>ground beef (or bison)</span>
            </li>
            </ul>
</div>
                </div>

            <div id="recipe-preparation-container" class="mt-3">

                    <div id="recipe-directions" class="mb-4">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-capitalize">How To Make italian stuffed zucchini</h2>

        
        <ul id="recipe-preparation" class="list-unstyled">
            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/IeEBuk5RQE3xcIxVyXCZtDCkV3pA1_WWkx8O_5_CpwDA3n0-wItsDQOcUHK0KS1VzMaMrDOtVm7WgcCU6lcPeiw3-Bbqk3s_dCnbzuW7=w750"
                             alt="Cooking onions and garlic in a skillet."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 1</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">SAUCE: Heat olive oil in a very large skillet over medium to medium-high heat. Add onions and cook until they are soft and translucent (not browned). Add garlic and cook for 1 minute more.</div>

                </li>

            
                        <div id="link-box-wrapper" class="ad-unit-wrap rounded no-print">
            <div id="link-box" class="doli-added ad-container ad-loading ad-unit text-center"></div>
        </div>
        
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/LoE1Ornrl7Uh0PwQAMvX-6LuW0adiLjnM0DFI6yR5B9OsKGpsKhfenfW4h-oL5e4NVd_GqlmQRjviH4fUQq5m1gSQCtAlrrZzixJ1a0=w750"
                             alt="Tomatoes added to the onions."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 2</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">Carefully add tomatoes and salt (they will splatter!). If using canned whole tomatoes, crush them with your hands as they go in. Lower heat and simmer, stirring occasionally, for 15 minutes.</div>

                </li>

            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/7H_3Cinz2EwdpoF6Y7CkuTNch8SGnQnGtbe6-BBGK_ZrujjCULO-EJNtS50IWoQjAcKkCxeI3REI6-y5gQ8E7SfPlJLWiq97_grE8XU=w750"
                             alt="Eggs, Parmesan, Italian seasoning, garlic, salt, parsley, and bread pieces in a bowl."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 3</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">MEATBALLS: Wet slices of bread and quickly squeeze out the moisture. Shred the bread into a large bowl. Add eggs, Parmesan (use low fat if desired), Italian seasoning, garlic, salt, and chopped parsley and mix.</div>

                </li>

            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/T9DzV4FQ1eqZyQu8_EaH8kl7d6Jov_44xFfZrK3-5obpFjJPfdEiE0E7qoQ3jkpD6Uce4t88fgHAFUbEstZIH-5BE_ThDLSeR5oPlrW-=w750"
                             alt="Mixing in the ground beef."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 4</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">Add meat (use the bison for a lower fat content - no one will know!) and gently combine everything.</div>

                </li>

            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/KxH4tGWTG8xU5B2ds5NLaopFLmOyQMZ7zrlFUmtq4tVC9ziCw7hKpqay01l59FqFrkBhR7B6fVB-9HBz_yHqrD8A0lEoxiux_m1XJEw=w750"
                             alt="Removing the middle of the zucchini."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 5</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">COMPOSE: Slice the large zucchini into 2-inch drums. Using an apple corer, core out the center of the flesh containing seeds of each drum.</div>

                </li>

            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/0qct-Qfu9vgEhhbpGo2RRBksLVwTh1S6x-5Pyb8GF12tFw0H7ItnMLMAvkwaJEiZAHQ133b_gzabBdsiBmSclzomUMrf8YqHSN4aChA=w750"
                             alt="Stuffing the zucchini with the meat mixture."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 6</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">Gently stuff the meat mixture into each zucchini drum.</div>

                </li>

            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/QI_o61xnQLfKFUfE81GyvYs9tGFLfm0t9Dt0RVZlDJXaw-5aijxa8fSNGYudPrj8i-dzFCFN52AnJ5jTE6Ec8xlwUscVoOKaONrLEg=w750"
                             alt="Stuffed zucchini and meatballs simmering in the tomato sauce."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 7</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">Place them in the simmering sauce. Make meatballs with leftover meat mixture and place them in the simmering sauce. Cover and cook for approximately 25-30 minutes, turning the zucchini and meatballs one time, or until the meat is cooked through.</div>

                </li>

            
                
                <li class="card bg-transparent border-0 rcp-direction-item mx-auto mb-4">

                                        <div class="rounded bg-dark no-print position-relative animate-all mb-3" data-direction-image style="padding-top:67%;height:0;width:100%;">
                        <img src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAwACAIAAAP///////yH5BAUAAAEALAAAAAADAAIAAAIChF8AOw=="                              style="opacity:0.01; top:0; left:0; right: 0; bottom:0;"
                             data-aspect-ratio=".67"                              data-lazy-src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/Mf31K0fJFgbomwCySrXuSKmsKkR6s-Be7OykDG1JpVOE8fKuxJWSFMtaAq_N676yJiYYx3RN1ynsDsmrKQ5ZNtAC6xumlnUJ0tQBIJs=w750"
                             alt="Italian Stuffed Zucchini on a plate with spaghetti."
                             class="rounded fade-img w-100 h-100 position-absolute no-print " />
                    </div>



                    

                    <div class="font-weight-bold small text-uppercase">Step 8</div>
                    <div class="flex-fill recipe-direction rcp-ugc-block">Serve over spaghetti noodles with additional Parmesan cheese.</div>

                </li>

